Dear Zhong Miao,

Thank you for your report.

I have read the thread on the NANOGsec list, reviewed your github, and
conducted some further investigation.
I will start by highlighting the role of the RIRs in these cases.  
As the RIR, we are only responsible for ensuring that policies are being
applied in a fair and equitable way, that have been developed by the
community.  If there is no policy breach, then there is little the RIRs can do
in these instances.
But I will respond to your specific requests

Have you notified the affected APNIC members (China Telecom, Alibaba Cloud,
etc.) about this hijacking?
APNIC monitors hijack events via a member portal called DASH.  Members are
able to set alerts when routing data from multiple sources indicates that
there is a non conformance in their ROA states.  This is purely up to the
member to create these alerts.


Does APNIC have any mechanism to work with RIPE NCC and ARIN to prevent
cross-RIR origin hijacking?
The RIR's have good cross-communication with each other at a hostmaster and
registry level.

What guidance can APNIC provide to its members to better protect their
prefixes using RPKI/ROV, especially against origin hijacking?
APNIC frequently conducts ROA and RPKI training within the region. This
training is made available to all members.

I hope this answers your questions, and if you have anything further, I would
suggest that you contact our helpdesk on helpdesk@apnic.net


Regards


Dave Phelan
Policy Manager and Senior Network Analyst

